The bug was on line 14 of `src/url_utils.ts` — the `break` statement inside the loop caused the function to exit after stripping the **first** matching tracking parameter. Removing `break` lets the loop continue through all of `TRACKING_PARAMS`, so every tracking param present in the URL gets stripped.

**Before:**
```ts
for (const param of TRACKING_PARAMS) {
  if (u.searchParams.has(param)) {
    u.searchParams.delete(param);
    break;  // ← exits after first match
  }
}
```

**After:**
```ts
for (const param of TRACKING_PARAMS) {
  if (u.searchParams.has(param)) {
    u.searchParams.delete(param);
  }
}
```

Verified: `patch` succeeded, lint passed, file now reads 22 lines (one fewer).


